Z||000000||Loki||05-15-2001||12:33 AM||||OK, I think I have decided not to fight for custody of my son for now due to im not finacially stable enough. (yet)  And was wondering, Who decides visitaion and child support? The court or the parents?<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-15-2001||01:38 AM||||Usually the court decides the terms of the visitations. It depends on the state and the court about Child support. Some states have a set value, Some have a min and max value, and others are controlled by the court. There are also rules as to how the child support is used. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||05-15-2001||04:18 AM||||Loki, think we hashed this over before. <BR>But is she financially stable? Is she a good person. <BR>Sorry I'm a little cynical but when my ex and I broke up. I kind of let her have her way just to cause less waves and because she made more money. Well now it's been 2+ years since I've seen my son.. If you decide to let her have full custody. Make sure you get guaranteed visitation, it's not perfect but better than "reasonable visitation".. <BR>Word of advise.. It might get alot worse before it starts to get better. <BR>If this isn't your situation my apologies, just hate for anyone else to go through what I have.||||reg||1
